Name: hyperTalkCompatible

Type: property

Syntax: set the hyperTalkCompatible of <stack> to {true | false}

Syntax: get the hyperTalkCompatible of <stack>

Summary:
Specifies whether a <stack> <import|imported> from <HyperCard> sends
its messages the way <HyperCard> did.

Associations: stack

Introduced: 9.7.1

OS: mac, windows, linux, html5

Platforms: desktop, server

Example:
set the hyperTalkCompatible of stack "Address Book" to true

Example:
if the hyperTalkCompatible of this stack then answer "HyperCard rules"

Value (bool):
The <hyperTalkCompatible> of a <stack> is true or false. By default, it
is false.

Description:
Use the <hyperTalkCompatible> <property> to run a <stack> that came
from <HyperCard> with the rules its <script|scripts> were written for.
It changes nothing for a <stack> whose <hyperTalkCompatible> is false,
which is every <stack> unless a <script> sets it. File > Import Stack
sets it for each <stack> it imports, unless File > Import Stack >
HyperCard Message Order is turned off.

When it is true, three things are as they were in <HyperCard>, for the
<stack> and for its substacks:

- A message that a <control> of a <background> group does not handle
  goes to the <card> before the <background>: a background button's
  <mouseUp> reaches the card's <script>, then the background's, then
  the stack's.
- A <handler> can be called <doMenu>.
- The <doMenu> <command> is first sent as a message to the <object>
  whose <handler> runs it, with the menu item as its parameter. The
  menu item is chosen only if no <handler> takes the message, or one
  passes it.

The <stack> keeps the <property> as its <custom property> of the same
name, and is saved with it, so the <stack file> format does not change.
An engine without the <property> opens the <stack> with its usual
rules.

Set the <hyperTalkCompatible> before the <stack|stack's> <script|scripts>
are first compiled: a <script> already compiled keeps the <handler>
names it was compiled with until it is set again.

References: HCStack (property), HCAddressing (property),
HCImportStat (property), doMenu (command), import (command),
stack (object), background (glossary), message path (glossary),
HyperCard (glossary), custom property (glossary)
